{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Hark a traveler to the Land of the Rising Sun a journey most grand I shall weave for thee a course of days across that mystical land.\n\n**Day First Tokyo's Embrace**\n\nFrom distant shores thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's bright keep a city of wonders where ancient and modern do sleep. First visit the Imperial Palace a sight most regal and bold then wander through the gardens stories untold. Explore the vibrant markets of Tsukiji's domain where seafood delights doth ever remain. Ascend the Skytree a tower so high it doth pierce the clouds a view to enthrall all crowds. Dine upon sushi a culinary art so fine a taste of Japan truly divine.\n\n**Day Second Tokyo's Delights**\n\nTo Asakusa's temple we shall now proceed a place of peace where prayers are decreed.  Senso-ji's grandeur a sight to behold lanterns glow bright stories of old.  Then onward to Shibuya a crossing most famed where pedestrians surge a spectacle framed.  Harajuku's fashions a riot of hue young souls express their visions anew.  Shinjuku's gardens a tranquil escape from the city's rush a moment to shape.  Evening brings karaoke a joyful release a singing spree for ultimate peace.\n\n**Day Third Hakone's Beauty**\n\nA journey to Hakone a mountain retreat where nature's embrace is bittersweet. Cruise across Lake Ashi a vista so fair with Mount Fuji's grace beyond compare.  Ride the Hakone Ropeway a cable car's flight where volcanic fumes paint the sky bright.  Explore the Hakone Open-Air Museum sculptures abound a blend of art profound.  Stay in a Ryokan a traditional inn where tatami mats and futons begin.  Enjoy an onsen a hot spring's warm grace a soothing balm for time and space.\n\n**Day Fourth Kyoto's Ancient Heart**\n\nBy bullet train swift we shall now fly to Kyoto's old heart a city of grace and might.  Visit Fushimi Inari Shrine a path of red gates a mystical sight.  Explore Kiyomizu-dera Temple a wooden stage with views that engage.  Wander Gion's district where geishas reside a glimpse of a world where secrets hide.  Nijo Castle's grandeur a shogun's abode where history's echoes freely flowed.  Dine on Kaiseki cuisine a multi-course feast a culinary art bestowed.\n\n**Day Fifth Kyoto's Gardens**\n\nArashiyama Bamboo Grove a verdant delight where sunlight filters in dappled light.  Tenryu-ji Temple's garden a landscape serene a peaceful haven truly keen.  Kinkaku-ji's Golden Pavilion a shimmering gleam a reflection of a waking dream.  Ryoan-ji's rock garden a puzzle to solve a meditative role.  Attend a tea ceremony a ritual so refined a moment of stillness for heart and mind.  Explore Nishiki Market a culinary treasure trove where local delicacies freely rove.\n\n**Day Sixth Nara's Deer**\n\nA day trip to Nara where friendly deer roam free a sight to behold for thee.  Todai-ji Temple's Great Buddha a statue so grand a wonder to see.  Kasuga Taisha Shrine lanterns abound a path to enlightenment profound.  Interact with the deer a gentle embrace a moment of joy in this sacred space.  Return to Kyoto with memories so sweet a journey complete a wondrous feat.\n\n**Day Seventh Farewell Japan**\n\nWith heavy heart we bid farewell to this land of the sun a journey well done.  Depart from Kansai International Airport a memory made a chapter begun.  May thy spirit be filled with the beauty thou hast seen a treasure to keep. Until we meet again in realms serene and keen farewell Japan farewell sleep.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.011765611357986927}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.5393308401107788}, {"token": "▁traveler", "logprob": -2.0365824699401855}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.2189556062221527}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.5753092169761658}, {"token": "▁Land", "logprob": -0.6330228447914124}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.0486305914